<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44447" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐμένεια</span></b> , ἡ, poet.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐμελ-ία</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Pi.
			<u>P.</u>
			12.4
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>goodwill,
				favour</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμῖν . . παρὰ τῶν θεῶν . . εὐ. εἴη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.45
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				631
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				313
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Ap.</u>
				7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				197d
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ πρὸς τὸ θεῖον
			εὐ.</span> the <i>favour</i> of the gods (v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				5.105
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ συναντωμένη τισὶν εὐ. παρὰ τοῦ
					δαιμονίον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>SIG</u>
					601.14
				</span></i>
			 (Teos, <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ᾽
				εὐμενείᾳ</span> to gain <i>favour</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Tox.</u>
				1
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σὺν εὐμενίᾳ</span>
			<i>kindly</i>, Pi.l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of smell, <i>pleasantness</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				6.14.12
			</span></i>.</div>
